Reading through this thread I think there are too many variables (or
uncertainties) to make this work.
- There may be a problem with memory
- the hardware configuration may be incorrect (Q-bus sequence)
- the quality of the RD54 disks is still unknown (but they are both
suspect)
- the SYSGEN parameters for ADAMA on MASTER are set but some of them
have non-standard values
- there is no entry for the tertiary loader in the LANCP output.

All we know for sure is that the simh host works.

Another question comes up: how is the /uVAX II connected to the LAN?
The DEQNA/DELQA has AUI only IIRC so you must use a transceiver,
right?
Now I'm guessing here but could that be an Allied Telesys UTP
transceiver (or a similar product)?
If so, does it have a "heartbeat" or "squelch" switch (the Allied
Telesys transceivers have this switch).
Note its current position an switch it to the other. Try the boot
process again.

Should that fail, I'd recommend trying to boot the /uVAX II as a
diskless client.
Remove all hardware other than the ethernet board, or place a Qbus
terminator immediately after it.
rerun CLUSTER_CONFIG_LAN and select DECnet instead of LANCP.
Give us the output of the CLUSTER_CONFIG_LAN dialogue, the output of
MC NCP SHO KNOW CIRC CHAR and
MC NCP SHO NODE ADAMA CHAR

Hans


