Faulty memory would show an error during power up self tests.
Insufficient memory would show an error during boot.


> conclusion but what bothers me is the lack of error messages. The
> system boots, no errors and the OP gets a clean srm prompt, did I get
> that right?

The system powers up.
The Boot command is issued
The MOP request is received and processeed by the Boot node
The MV II then "crashes" with a console error message before VMS has had
the time to issue any text to the console.


> If so there's something else wrong. Hence the suggestion to move to
> DECnet and good old NCP where you can turn on monitoring events.

We already know that the boot node succesfully receives and serves the
MOP request according to the OP. LANCP issues messages to OPCOM when it
processes those messages.  No need for Decnet.


