H Vlems wrote:

> OK, that is as watertight as can be. But the microVAX II doesn't boot.
> What can we come up with to make the II boot VMS?

My guess is that the NISCS_LOAD needs more physical memory than is
available.

Another aspect is that the default settings in VAXVMSSYS.PAR may be way
overboard for a 4 meg system.  Cluster config can't know about the
hardware config of the satellite node, so it would have some default
template for it, and when the satellite node boots the first time, it
runs a bunch of things including autogen to tailor the environment to
the memory etc.

To the OP: The memory boards take their power from the QBUS, but there
is a ribbon cable which connects the memory to the CPU board.  Also, I
am not sure how the QBUS should be configured if you do not have the 2
memory boards in there (can they be used by other devices, or must they
be left empty, or must a grant card be put in there ?)

Worse comes to worse, I could ship 16 meg memory to the OP.

What I could try (in a couple of weeks) is to take one of my 2 MVIIs,
and try to MOP boot them without any memory connected and see what error
message I get.

