Elderico wrote:

> - how (if ever possible) to install OpenVMS locally on the uVax from
> the cluster


If the satellite node MVII has its swap/page files on the boot node
(aka: its own disk is unused), then it is fairly simple to install VMS
on it:

MOUNT/FOREIGN disk2:  (the MVII's disk)
BACKUP/IMAGE/IGNORE=INTERLOCK/LOG/NOALIAS  disk1: disk2:

where disk1 is your system disk in the SIMH node, and disk2 is the disk
on the MVII.

SHOW DEV D will give you the disk names. This command can be executed
from either node.

Normally, you would want each node in a cluster to have a different:

SCSNODE	      (6 characters)
SCSSYSTEMID   (number derived from decnet address)
ALLOCLASS

The ALLOCLASS is a number that is added to each disk device. so DUA0
becomes $5$DUA0 if the alloclass is set to 5 on a node.

This way, if both nodes have a disk called DUA0: then the two defines
end with with different names and it is then possible to differentiate them.


