You need some kind of load medium.  An InfoServer would do, but
perhaps the Simh-based host will not.  I suspect that loading the
.B saveset onto the target disk beforehand is enough, though.
Once you boot to it it should start the install process and
ask where the savesets are located.  A DECnet reference might
work once you have given the install function the DECnet address
you will be using for your new install.  This is speculation on
my part - I have long forgotten how to do anything other than
a plain vanilla install on a VAX.

But I don't see why you would need a clean install. CLUSTER_CONFIG
will clone the VMS boot instance on the Simh host, and if that
is not considered good enough, a clean install on that host
could be done first.  Once you had a local boot disk you could
do with it as you liked, including turning off clustering and
performing system management tasks locally.

George Cornelius


