The simh system contains the VMS kit (VMS073.*) and its disks are
accessible by the /uVAX II as long as it is part of the cluster.
The reason for a clean install is the RD54's limited capacity: 154 MB.
We have no idea what size the emulated system disk of the simh host
is.
Without that knowledge it doesn't make sense to me to advise the OP to
do an image backup.
It might not fit on the RD54, unless he'se running MASTER off an RZ23L
or smaller, which I doubt.
Just installing the VMS073.B saveset makes the target system dependent
on network access to get to the other VMS073.% files. Given the
problems we've had to get this far seems a bit too much.
In case just one RD54 is working then the OP ought to create an RZ23L
disk (121 MB). If an image backup of the simh system disk fits on it,
then no problem: that same backup will fit on the RD54. If it doesn't
fit the the OP must either TAILOROFF the current system disk, or
reduce page-, dump- and swapfile sizes.
An alternative is a clean install on the simh system and select only
the minimal part needed to run VMS.


