Elderico wrote:
>> SHOW DEV D will give you the disk names. This command can be executed
>> from either node.
> 
> ok, one more step ahead: after some jumper swapping on the rqdx board
> and disks, I finally managed to have the uVax recognize them. Having
> set ALLOCLASS to 1 for ADAMA, I now can see them listed with SHOW DEV
> D as $1$DUA0: and $1$DUA1:
> 
> the only doubt I have is I don't get anything for these devices in the
> "volume label" column, nor if I call SHOW DEV/FULL on those devices.
> Is this a hint that those devices are not initialized? Is there any
> other way to check if there is any data on those disks? (I'm thinking
> of something like `cfdisk` command on linux systems)

You only state RQDX board, so I am not sure which one you have.

If you want to use RD54s, you MUST have an RQDX3.

Are these actually RD54s?  The RD54 is a rebadged Maxtor 2190.

The DS (Device Select) settings on the RD54s is important.

What they need to be set to depends on whether or not you are using a 
RQDXE expander board.

With the expander board the DS for both drives should be set to the 
third device.  I think the RD54 labels the pins 1, 2, 3, and 4, so you 
need to jumper 3 to C (with no other device select jumpers).  If they 
are labeled 0, 1, 2, 3, jumper ID 2.

Without the expander board, I don't remember how the RD54s need to be 
jumpered.

Have these drives been used on some machine other than a MicroVAX II? 
If they have, they will need to be formatted.  Unfortunately, the 
MicroVAX II ROMs are not smart enough to format this drive.

On a MicroVAX II, the formatting was done by a diagnostic tape.  (This 
was generally a TK50.)  Only certain versions of the tape could format 
an RD54.

Good luck!

