Elderico wrote:

> another option I didn't consider is to make an OpenVMS install on a
> simh emulated vax, and then netboot the real one from there.. would it
> be simpler?

Yes. Because the simh VAX will support clustering and SCS, so after the
initial MOP  file is sent to the booting vax, the later can sart SCS and
access "its" system disk to complete the booting.

When you configure the satellite node (using cluster_config in the
simh), make sure that the page/swap files are located on the simh unit.
This leaves the all mighty Microvax II's disk free. Once booted, you can
then backup/image to the drive.


