You must have done right, most of the things at least. The simh based
boothost recognized the network frame that initiated the download.
It sent NISCS_LOAD.EXE, that's a good thing. So the MAC address is
correctly loaded in MASTER's NCP database.
The DECnet circuit on MASTER has the service attribute enabled,
otherwise the load wouldn't have been succesful.
But ADAMA seems unable to do anything useful with the loader.
I must admit that I haven't seen a microVAX II since 2001, so perhaps
JF Mezei can tell us whether the Boot command on the /uVAV II needs
more information.
Could you give us the output for this command:

MC NCP SHO NODE ADAMA CHAR

The output must be similar to this:
Remote node =3D  1.20
(ADAMA)                                                       ! the
DECnet address is a dummy of course

Hardware address           =3D 08-00-2b-xx-xx-xx
Tertiary loader                =3D SYS$SYSTEM:TERTIARY_VMB.EXE
Load assist agent           =3D SYS$SHARE:NISCS_LAA.EXE               !
may be NISCS_LOAD since this is a VMS V6 manual :-(
Load assist parameter    =3D DISK$OVMSVAXSYS:<SYS10.>             ! from
your own information.


The DECnet address for ADAMA is in the same area as MASTER, right?
Hans


